       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1000 mg is five times the maximum recommended sertraline dose of 200 mg/day. At that dose there's a serious risk of serotonin syndrome, seizures, and QT prolongation.\n\nWas this meant to be one of these?\n\n- **100 mg PO once daily**, which is a common maintenance dose.\n- **50 mg PO once daily**, which is the usual starting dose for depression and anxiety.\n- **200 mg PO once daily**, which is the maximum dose.\n\nTell me the dose you intended and I'll enter it right away. If you really do want 1000 mg, for example as part of a monitored protocol, tell me that and give me a note for the order. I'd still advise confirming it with pharmacy first."
      }
